 of the birthday cake your mom made you, or, you know, you talk about the mole recipe that

00:38:07.450 --> 00:38:11.810
 your mom made with your brother that started this whole, yeah.

00:38:11.910 --> 00:38:16.750
 Thinking about these things, but that I need those things in my life.

00:38:16.790 --> 00:38:22.680
 Those are like real locations that make me know where I am in relationship to things.

00:38:23.240 --> 00:38:24.420
 What do you think about that?

00:38:24.500 --> 00:38:26.780
 Where, how does that come into play?

00:38:28.100 --> 00:38:35.450
 Well, I just, I'm, I'm trying to just in hearing you sort of try to talk about this.

00:38:35.550 --> 00:38:36.710
 I mean, there's different things.

00:38:36.770 --> 00:38:43.640
 I don't know quite sure if that's going to answer your question, but there was a, when I did,

00:38:43.640 --> 00:38:47.080
 I did the installation at the LA public library.

00:38:47.080 --> 00:38:50.840
 I did an installation of the prison gourmet last year.

